,title,link,text,language,family
0,Austronesian peoples - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austronesian_peoples,"The Austronesian peoples, sometimes referred to as Austronesian-speaking peoples, [45] are a large collection of peoples who speak Austronesian languages, having settled in Taiwan, maritime Southeast Asia, parts of mainland Southeast Asia, Micronesia, coastal New Guinea, Island Melanesia, Polynesia, and Madagascar. [46][47] They also include indigenous ethnic minorities in Vietnam, Cambodia ...",Kaidipang,Austronesian
1,Musik Remix Lagu Daerah Kaidipang - Koleksi Terbaru Full Album,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FBbcqawW74A,"Album ini menawarkan musikal bahasa daerah Kaidipang dengan aransemen yang menyentuh hati. Setiap lagu berfungsi sebagai jendela budaya, membawa pendengar untuk memahami nilai-nilai tradisional ...",Kaidipang,Austronesian
2,Austronesian Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/@austronesianmusic6149,"Hi everyone! Welcome to Austronesian Music🎶This channel mainly posts music from Austronesian countries and languages, and also other songs of languages of Southeast Asia.",Kaidipang,Austronesian
3,Austronesian Music - Melodigging,https://www.melodigging.com/genre/austronesian-music,"Austronesian music is an umbrella term for the diverse musical traditions of Austronesian-speaking peoples, whose homelands stretch from Taiwan through Island Southeast Asia to Oceania and Madagascar.",Kaidipang,Austronesian
4,Austronesian Soundscapes: Performing Arts in Oceania and ... - JSTOR,https://www.jstor.org/stable/j.ctt46mvnd,"Austronesian Soundscapes is a collection of essays on Austronesian musics that transcends disciplinary frontiers in the humanities and social sciences. In all of Austronesia, music plays a crucial role in the negotiation of cultural identities; yet research on the diversity of the Austronesian cultural belt's music has hitherto been rather sparse.",Kaidipang,Austronesian
5,Kaidipang language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/kaidipang_language,"Kaidipang is an Austronesian language of the Gorontalic subgroup, spoken by approximately 6,700 people (as of 2023) primarily in the Bolaang Mongondow Utara regency of North Sulawesi, Indonesia. [1][2][3] It serves as the primary language of the Kaidipang people, who inhabit villages along the north coast and highlands near Bolaangitang town, engaging in rice farming, fishing, and livestock ...",Kaidipang,Austronesian
6,Austronesian Soundscapes: Performing Arts in Oceania and Southeast Asia,https://www.iias.asia/books/austronesian-soundscapes-performing-arts-oceania-and-southeast-asia,"Drawing together contemporary cultural studies and musical analysis, Austronesian Soundscapes will fill this research gap, offering a comprehensive analysis of traditional and contemporary Austronesian music and, at the same time, investigating how music reflects the challenges that Austronesian cultures face in this age of globalization.",Kaidipang,Austronesian
7,Austronesian Soundscapes - Cambridge University Press & Assessment,https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/austronesian-soundscapes/8B714F18DC010F5F8E4997353C4B18BA,"Drawing together contemporary cultural studies and musical analysis, Austronesian Soundscapes will fill this research gap, offering a comprehensive analysis of traditional and contemporary Austronesian music and, at the same time, investigating how music reflects the challenges that Austronesian cultures face in this age of globalization.",Kaidipang,Austronesian
8,Austronesian Music - Music genre - Rate Your Music,https://rateyourmusic.com/genre/austronesian-music/,"Austronesian music nowadays refers to the ongoing evolution and fusion of various cultural influences from foreign and neighbouring cultures. These influences have over the centuries introduced new instruments, styles, and genres, blending age-old elements with newer traditions.",Kaidipang,Austronesian
9,ABVD: Kaidipang,https://abvd.eva.mpg.de/austronesian/language.php?id=29,"Austronesian Basic Vocabulary Database Language: Kaidipang ... Resources: Ethnologue Information for kzp OLAC Information for kzp [Suggest a resource] Change History: Changed from ""kidontorʔu"" (Word 187) - Laurie Reid (2016-07-21 09:29:12) Changed from ""rʔima"" (Word 1) - Laurie Reid (2016-06-15 09:35:00)",Kaidipang,Austronesian
